# Lesson 2, from the point-count exercise hand 10.
title: Short suits help you open
id: L02-15
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.1, 2.6
student: S
board: 15
dealer: S
vulnerable: NS

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  853    K82    KJ64   Q85
  E  T962   Q54    A2     A643
  S  K4     AJ6    QT9753 J7
  W  AQJ7   T973   8      KT92

auction:
  S 1D*    = 13+ points, at least four diamonds
     key: 11 HCP plus 1 for each doubleton is 13, with six diamonds. Open 1♦.
     not Pass: Did you count your doubletons? They bring you to 13.
     not 2D: A two-bid shows 22+ points. Did you count 13?
     not *: With 13 points and six diamonds, which opening shows them?
  W Pass
  N 2D     = 6-9 points and diamond support
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = No game: at most 22
     key: Partner showed 6-9. Your 13 plus 9 is 22 at most, and a diamond game needs about 28.
     not 3D: Did you add it up? 13 plus 6-9 is far short of a diamond game.
     not 2NT: Did you add it up? 13 plus 6-9 can't reach 25.
     not 3NT: Did you add it up? 13 plus 6-9 can't reach 25.
  W Pass

auction recap:
  Your two doubletons lifted 11 HCP to 13, enough to open. Partner's 2♦
  showed 6-9 points and diamond support. Your side has at most 22, and a
  game in diamonds needs about 28, so you pass. You are declarer, because
  you bid diamonds first, and so West will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  trumps out: 3
  remind: What is the contract? How many tricks do you need?

play:
  1   W HT  N H2  E HQ  S HA
  2   S D3  W D8  N DK  E DA
      note: The plan: draw trumps, take your heart winners, then trump clubs. Start with a trump to dummy's king.
  3   E ST  S SK  W SA  N S3
  4   W SQ  N S5  E S2  S S4
  5   W SJ  N S8  E S6  S D9
      note: You have no spades left, so trump.
  6   S DT  W C2  N D4  E D2
      note: Draw East's last trump.
  7   S HJ  W H3  N H8  E H4
      note: Now your heart winners.
  8   S H6  W H7  N HK  E H5
      note: A heart to dummy's ♥K.
  9   N C5  E C3  S CJ  W CK
      note: Lead a club. You have to lose some clubs anyway.
  10  W CT  N CQ  E CA  S C7
  11  E C4  S D5  W C9  N C8
      note: Trump it.
  12  S DQ  W H9  N D6  E C6
      note: Take your trumps.
  13  S D7  W S7  N DJ  E S9
      note: The last trump. 8 tricks: 2♦ made.

play recap:
  The plan: draw trumps, take your heart winners, then trump clubs.

  2♦ made exactly. Partner's raise and your pass kept you in a safe part
  score.
